### Page 1 of 1

```text
RESOLUTION NO.  ________

ENTITLED:  “A RESOLUTION AUTHORIZING SUBMISSION OF A FEDERAL
MINERAL ROYALTY CAPITAL CONSTRUCTION ACCOUNT GRANT
APPLICATION TO THE STATE LOAN AND INVESTMENT BOARD ON
BEHALF OF THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
FOR THE PURPOSE OF THE COMPLETING THE 26TH STREET
INTERCEPTOR PROJECT.”

WHEREAS, the Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne (“City”) desires to participate
in the Federal Mineral Royalty Capital Construction Account Grant program to assist in
financing the 26th Street Interceptor Project (“Project”); and

WHEREAS, the City recognizes the need for the Project; and

WHEREAS, the Project will be part of the overall Capitol Basin Flood Control Project,
and the Project will also include the addition of new water mains; and

WHEREAS, the Federal Mineral Royalty Capital Construction Account Grant program
requires that certain criteria be met, as described in the State Loan and Investment Board’s Rules
governing the program and to the best of the City’s knowledge this application meets those
criteria; and

WHEREAS, grant funding for this Project will be considered by the State Loan and
Investment Board at its meeting on January 19, 2017; and

WHEREAS, the total estimated Project cost is Five Million Three Hundred Twelve
Thousand Seven Hundred Thirty Dollars ($5,312,730.00), and the City requests a grant of One
Million Seven Hundred Seventy Thousand Seven Hundred Thirty Dollars ($1,770,730.00) and
plans to match the requested Federal Mineral Royalty Capital Construction Account Grant with
Two Million Nine Hundred Forty-Two Thousand Dollars ($2,942,000.00) from an Economic
Development Administration (EDA) grant and Six Hundred Thousand Dollars ($600,000.00) of
Board of Public Utilities funds, totaling a match of Three Million Five Hundred Forty-Two
Thousand Dollars ($3,542,000.00).

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE
CITY OF CHEYENNE, that the City is authorized to submit a Federal Mineral Royalty Capital
Construction Account Grant application for One Million Seven Hundred Seventy Thousand
Seven Hundred Thirty Dollars ($1,770,730.00) to the State Loan and Investment Board for
consideration at the January 19, 2017 State Loan and Investment Board meeting to assist in
funding the 26th Street Interceptor Project.

BE IT FURTHER RESOLVED, that the Mayor of the City of Cheyenne, is hereby
designated as the authorized representative of the City to act on behalf of the Governing Body on
all matters relating to this grant application.

PRESENTED, READ, AND ADOPTED THIS ______ day of ___________, 2016.

Richard L. Kaysen, Mayor

(SEAL)

Attest:

Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk
```
